<%# Choosing the new password, reached from the emailed link. #344.

    One box, matching views/create-account.erb, and for the reason recorded there: this app
    turns off Rodauth's confirmation fields, so a second box would be rejected for a
    parameter the form does not send. autocomplete="new-password" asks a password manager to
    generate and keep the credential rather than leaving a human to type it twice -- which
    matters a little less here than it did before #344, since a typo now costs another reset
    email rather than the account. %>
<div class="flex min-h-full flex-col justify-center px-6 py-12 lg:px-8">
  <div class="sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <h1 class="text-center text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Choose a new password</h1>
    <%== render('_form_error') %>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <form method="post" class="space-y-6" role="form" id="reset-password-form" autocomplete="on">
      <%== rodauth.csrf_tag %>
      <%# No hidden key field, and that is the point rather than an omission. Rodauth answers
          the emailed link with a redirect to this route without the query string, having put
          the token in the session on the way past -- so the secret leaves the address bar
          and cannot escape through a Referer header on whatever loads next. By the time this
          form renders, the key is session state and the form has nothing to carry. %>
      <div>
        <label for="password" class="block text-sm font-medium leading-6 text-gray-900">New password</label>
        <div class="mt-2">
          <input id="password" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" required
                 class="<%= field_style %> block w-full py-1.5 text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400 sm:text-sm sm:leading-6">
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <button type="submit" class="<%= button_style %> flex w-full justify-center bg-lime-500 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">Save it and sign in</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
